# Upstream C++ members that deliberately have no binding on the downstream surface.
#
# Read by check_api_drift.ps1, which fails on any public member of a mapped class that
# reaches no binding. Format, one per line:
#
#     <pair id>  <Type>::<Member>     # why it is not exposed
#
# The key is the PAIR plus the member, so exempting something from the C ABI says
# nothing about whether a COM server should carry it. That distinction is the reason
# there are three of these files across the three repositories rather than one shared
# list: MsgFacade answers a different question about the same class than Msgcore_c.h
# does, and a shared exemption would quietly answer both.
#
# A REASON IS NOT DECORATION. The C API is a deliberate subset, and the argument this
# repository has never written down anywhere is WHICH subset and why. Each line here is
# one sentence of that argument, and the next reader should be able to tell whether it
# still holds. "Internal" on its own is not a reason; "takes a P2PmsgHANDLE, which is
# not a type the flat surface has" is.
#
# UNTRIAGED marks a line banked by -Seed on the day the check was first run. It means
# only that nobody has looked yet. The count is printed on every run for the reason the
# register keeps relearning -- a number nobody prints is a number nobody reads -- and
# working it down is the actual product of this check.
#
# There is one thing this file cannot do: it cannot notice that a binding's BEHAVIOUR
# drifted from the C++ it wraps. msgcore_mgr_load began refusing stored images that
# 0278981's walks now judge, with no signature change and no line here. Only a test
# catches that, and none did.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  UNTRIAGED -- banked by -Seed, not decided by anybody.
#
#  Each line below says only that the member had no counterpart on the day the
#  check was first run. Replacing UNTRIAGED with a real reason IS the triage, and
#  the count is printed on every run so the backlog cannot go quiet.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
